### Lines 100–139: The Task Modal

```html
<div class="modal-overlay" id="taskModal">
    <div class="modal">
        <h2 class="modal-title" id="modalTitle">Add Task</h2>
        
        <div class="form-group">
            <label>Title</label>
            <input type="text" id="taskTitle" placeholder="Enter task title...">
        </div>
        
        <div class="form-group">
            <label>Due Date</label>
            <input type="date" id="taskDueDate">
        </div>
        
        <div class="form-group">
            <label>Subtasks</label>
            <div class="subtasks-list" id="subtasksList"></div>
            <button class="add-subtask-btn" id="addSubtaskBtn">+ Add Subtask</button>
        </div>
        
        <div class="form-group">
            <label>Info</label>
            <div class="info-toolbar">
                <button data-command="bold"><b>B</b></button>
                <button data-command="italic"><i>I</i></button>
                <button data-command="underline"><u>U</u></button>
                <button data-command="strikethrough"><s>S</s></button>
                <button data-command="insertUnorderedList">•</button>
                <button data-command="insertOrderedList">1.</button>
            </div>
            <div class="info-editor" id="infoEditor" contenteditable="true"></div>
        </div>
        
        <div class="modal-actions">
            <button class="btn btn-danger" id="deleteTaskBtn" style="display:none;">Delete</button>
            <button class="btn btn-secondary" id="cancelBtn">Cancel</button>
            <button class="btn btn-primary" id="saveTaskBtn">Save</button>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
```

#### What is a Modal?
A **modal** (or dialog box) is a popup that appears on top of the page. It blocks interaction with the rest of the page until it's closed. Here:
- `.modal-overlay` is the dark semi-transparent background
- `.modal` is the white box in the center

#### `<input type="text">` vs `<input type="date">`
The `type` attribute changes how the input behaves:
- `type="text"` → Free-form text field
- `type="date"` → A calendar date picker (built into the browser!)
- `type="checkbox"` → A tick box

#### `placeholder="Enter task title..."`
Placeholder text shown when the input is empty — it disappears when you start typing.

#### `contenteditable="true"`
This attribute on **any** HTML element makes it editable by the user, like a textarea but with rich text support. Combined with `document.execCommand()`, it acts as a basic word processor.

#### `style="display:none;"`
This is an **inline style** — CSS written directly on an element. It hides the "Delete" button. When editing a task, JavaScript sets it to `display:block` to show it.

#### `data-command="bold"`
Used by the rich text toolbar buttons. JavaScript reads this attribute to know which formatting command to apply.

