### 3.3.12 View Toggle (Lines 361–373)

```javascript
document.querySelectorAll('.view-btn').forEach(btn => {
    btn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        document.querySelectorAll('.view-btn').forEach(b => b.classList.remove('active'));
        btn.classList.add('active');
        
        const view = btn.dataset.view;
        document.getElementById('kanbanView').classList.toggle('active', view === 'kanban');
        document.getElementById('calendarView').classList.toggle('active', view === 'calendar');
        currentView = view;
        
        if (view === 'calendar') renderCalendar();
    });
});
```

#### `querySelectorAll('.view-btn')`
Returns a **NodeList** (array-like collection) of all elements with class `view-btn`. Regular CSS selector syntax.

#### `classList.toggle('active', condition)`
- `.classList.add('class')` → Adds a class
- `.classList.remove('class')` → Removes a class
- `.classList.toggle('class', bool)` → Adds if `bool` is `true`, removes if `false`

The CSS for `.kanban-view.active` sets `display: flex`. Without the `.active` class, it's `display: none`.

