### 3.3.15 Rich Text Editor (Lines 441–446)

```javascript
document.querySelectorAll('.info-toolbar button').forEach(btn => {
    btn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        document.execCommand(btn.dataset.command, false, null);
        document.getElementById('infoEditor').focus();
    });
});
```

#### `document.execCommand(command, showUI, value)`
A legacy but widely-supported browser API for rich text editing inside a `contenteditable` element.
- `'bold'` → Wraps selected text in `<b>` tags
- `'italic'` → Wraps in `<i>` tags
- `'insertUnorderedList'` → Creates a `<ul>` bullet list
- `'insertOrderedList'` → Creates an `<ol>` numbered list

The toolbar buttons have `data-command="bold"` etc., so `btn.dataset.command` gives us the right command to pass.

