### 3.3.16 Saving a Task (Lines 452–487)

```javascript
document.getElementById('saveTaskBtn').addEventListener('click', () => {
    const title = document.getElementById('taskTitle').value.trim();
    if (!title) {
        alert('Please enter a title');
        return;
    }
    
    const dueDate  = document.getElementById('taskDueDate').value;
    const info     = document.getElementById('infoEditor').innerHTML;
    const subtasks = getSubtasksFromForm();
    
    if (editingTaskId) {
        // EDIT MODE: find existing task and update it
        const task = tasks.find(t => t.id === editingTaskId);
        if (task) {
            task.title    = title;
            task.dueDate  = dueDate;
            task.info     = info;
            task.subtasks = subtasks;
        }
    } else {
        // ADD MODE: create a new task and push to array
        tasks.push({
            id:        generateId(),
            title,
            status:    'todo',
            dueDate,
            info,
            subtasks,
            createdAt: new Date().toISOString()
        });
    }
    
    saveTasks().then(() => {
        modal.classList.remove('active');  // Close modal
        render();                          // Re-render UI
    });
});
```

#### `.trim()`
Removes whitespace from both ends of a string: `"  hello  ".trim()` → `"hello"`.

#### `return;` inside a function
Exits the function early. Here, if there's no title, we show an alert and stop.

#### `tasks.push({...})`
`.push()` adds an element to the **end** of an array.

