### 3.3.17 Deleting a Task (Lines 489–497)

```javascript
document.getElementById('deleteTaskBtn').addEventListener('click', () => {
    if (confirm('Delete this task?')) {
        tasks = tasks.filter(t => t.id !== editingTaskId);
        saveTasks().then(() => {
            modal.classList.remove('active');
            render();
        });
    }
});
```

`tasks.filter(t => t.id !== editingTaskId)` → Creates a new array with all tasks **except** the one with the matching ID. `!==` means "not equal to".

