### 3.3.18 Closing Modal on Overlay Click (Lines 499–503)

```javascript
modal.addEventListener('click', (e) => {
    if (e.target === modal) {   // Only if clicked on the overlay itself
        modal.classList.remove('active');
    }
});
```

Clicking the dark background (overlay) closes the modal. The check `e.target === modal` ensures clicking inside the white modal box doesn't close it.

---

### 3.3.19 Utility Functions (Lines 505–514)

#### `escapeHtml(text)` — Security Function
```javascript
function escapeHtml(text) {
    const div = document.createElement('div');
    div.textContent = text;
    return div.innerHTML;
}
```
**Why do we need this?** If a task title contained `<script>alert('hacked')</script>`, injecting it as `innerHTML` would run the script (called **XSS — Cross-Site Scripting**).

The trick: set it as `.textContent` (plain text, no HTML parsing), then read `.innerHTML` — the browser automatically escapes the characters:
- `<` → `&lt;`
- `>` → `&gt;`
- `"` → `&quot;`

This is now safe to use in `innerHTML`.

#### `formatDate(dateStr)`
```javascript
function formatDate(dateStr) {
    const date = new Date(dateStr);
    return date.toLocaleDateString('en-US', {month: 'short', day: 'numeric'});
}
// "2026-03-10" → "Mar 10"
```

`toLocaleDateString(locale, options)` formats a date in a human-readable way. Options:
- `month: 'short'` → "Mar"
- `month: 'long'` → "March"
- `year: 'numeric'` → "2026"
- `day: 'numeric'` → "10"

