# PART 4: CSS Deep Dive ([css/styles.css](file:///c:/Users/Harsh%20Y%20Dhakan/Desktop/php%20stuff/css/styles.css))

## 4.1 The Reset
```css
* {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    box-sizing: border-box;
}
```
- `*` → Universal selector — targets EVERY element on the page
- `margin: 0; padding: 0;` → Browsers apply default margins/padding to elements (e.g., `<h1>` has default top margin). This removes all of them for consistency.
- `box-sizing: border-box;` → By default, CSS width excludes padding and border. `border-box` makes width include them. This prevents layout math headaches.

## 4.2 Layout: Flexbox (Kanban Board)
```css
.kanban-view.active {
    display: flex;      /* Activate flexbox */
    gap: 16px;          /* Space between columns */
    height: calc(100vh - 120px);  /* Full height minus header */
}

.column {
    flex: 1;    /* Each column takes equal share of space */
    min-width: 280px;
}
```

**Flexbox** is a CSS layout mode. When `display: flex` is set on a parent:
- Child elements (`columns`) become **flex items**
- They automatically arrange horizontally
- `flex: 1` makes each column take equal proportional space

`calc(100vh - 120px)` → CSS `calc()` allows math. `100vh` = 100% of the viewport height.

## 4.3 Layout: Grid (Calendar)
```css
.calendar-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(7, 1fr); /* 7 equal columns */
    gap: 1px;
    background: #e5e7eb;  /* Border color between cells */
}
```

**CSS Grid** is for two-dimensional layouts. `repeat(7, 1fr)` creates 7 columns each with `1fr` (one fraction of available space).

## 4.4 Show/Hide Pattern
```css
.kanban-view { display: none; }           /* Hidden by default */
.kanban-view.active { display: flex; }    /* Shown when .active class is added */

.modal-overlay { display: none; }
.modal-overlay.active { display: flex; }
```

JavaScript adds/removes the `.active` class. The CSS responds by showing/hiding the element.

## 4.5 Color Variables Used
```css
/* Background shades */
#f5f5f5 /* Light gray - page background */
#fff    /* White - cards, columns, modal */
#f9fafb /* Very light gray - hover states */
#f3f4f6 /* Light gray - badges */

/* Brand Colors */
#3b82f6 /* Blue - primary buttons, active state */
#22c55e /* Green - success */
#f59e0b /* Amber - warning ("soon" due date) */
#ef4444 /* Red - danger, overdue */

/* Text Colors */
#1f2937 /* Dark gray - main text */
#4b5563 /* Medium gray - labels */
#6b7280 /* Gray - secondary text */
#9ca3af /* Light gray - placeholders, disabled */

/* Borders */
#e5e7eb /* Very light gray - borders */
```

