# PART 5: The Data — [tasks.json](file:///c:/Users/Harsh%20Y%20Dhakan/Desktop/php%20stuff/tasks.json)

```json
[
    {
        "id": "mm9k04v9s0ecjqnj4d",
        "title": "Task 1",
        "status": "done",
        "dueDate": "",
        "info": "<b><u><i>this is a sample task</i></u></b>",
        "subtasks": [
            {
                "id": "mm9knu0uxr9kraw5a5m",
                "title": "first sbt",
                "done": false
            }
        ],
        "createdAt": "2026-03-02T19:10:15.717Z"
    }
]
```

JSON (JavaScript Object Notation) rules:
- Keys must be in **double quotes** (`"id"`, not `id`)
- Strings are in double quotes
- Numbers are bare (no quotes): `42`, `3.14`
- Booleans: `true` / `false` (lowercase)
- `null` for no value
- Arrays use `[]`, Objects use `{}`
- No trailing commas allowed

